From fc3727338cb1788c3ce06f338f59964b5442e9c6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: anyingiit <winshyon@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 17:34:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix: close singleton lock race between pidfile unlink and a
 starting daemon

SingletonLock.release() unlocked the pidfile before unlinking it, so a
daemon starting in that gap could lock the same inode, after which the
unlink left the next daemon free to create and lock a fresh pidfile:
two daemons running at once. A daemon that opened the pidfile before the
holder released and only reached flock() afterwards hit the same problem.

Unlink the pidfile while the lock is still held, and after acquiring the
lock verify (dev, inode) of the handle still matches the path, retrying on
a mismatch. Add regression tests for both interleavings.

Closes #1
